\DOC DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC

\TYPE {DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion asserts that a memory-access event trace lies
within given readable and writable address ranges.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t} whose conclusion is a
{memaccess_inbounds} claim relating an event list to a list of readable regions
and a list of writable regions, it solves the goal outright:
{
   A ?- t
   ========================  DISCHARGE_MEMACCESS_INBOUNDS_TAC
}
\noindent The event list may be built from {APPEND}/{CONS} of concrete load,
store and jump events, from abstract trace functions, or from {ENUMERATEL}
bodies. In the observed traces it succeeds both when the facts it needs
(nonoverlapping conditions, {memaccess_inbounds} claims about sub-traces,
symbolic machine state) occur among {A} and when the conclusion itself is
already an assumption.

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show only this outcome — the goal closed — and the inputs
are always {memaccess_inbounds} conclusions arising from symbolic-execution
states.

\ENDDOC
